# WAAMTO Website Version Management (Git)

Permanent. Applies to **ERP Website** (`waamto-website`) only.

## Branches

| Branch | Version | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `main` | Website Version 1 | Production (live) |
| `website-v2` | Website Version 2 | Development |

## Hard rules

- Never develop Version 2 on `main`.
- Never merge `website-v2` into `main` without explicit user approval.
- Never deploy `website-v2` unless the user explicitly says **Deploy Version 2**.
- Never deploy `main` unless the user explicitly says **Deploy Version 1**.
- Never mix V1 and V2 changes in one change set.
- If the version is ambiguous → **ask** before editing or deploying.

## User commands

| User says | Action |
| --- | --- |
| **Work on Version 1** | `git checkout main` → commit only to `main` |
| **Work on Version 2** | `git checkout website-v2` → commit only to `website-v2` |
| **Deploy Version 1** | Pull latest `main` → production build → deploy **main** to Webdock (build-only) |
| **Deploy Version 2** | Checkout `website-v2` → pull latest → build → deploy **website-v2** to Webdock **only** because user explicitly requested it |

Deploy scripts: `scripts/DEPLOY-WEBDOCK.md` / `scripts/deploy-website-build-only.ps1`  
Touch only `waamto-website` / PM2 `waamto-website`.

## Version intent

### Version 1 (`main`) — Production

- Live on Webdock
- **Allowed:** critical bugs, security, performance, content, production hotfixes
- **Forbidden:** major UI/UX redesign, experimental layout/illustration work

### Version 2 (`website-v2`) — Development

- Next-generation website
- All design / UI / UX / illustration / layout / typography / animation / redesign → here

## Approved release (only when user officially approves)

1. Merge `website-v2` into `main` (explicit approval required)
2. Tag release: `website-v2.0.0`
3. Deploy **main** to Webdock (as production)
4. After release: create `website-v3` — future development starts there

## Safety

- Do not assume which version to edit
- Do not auto-merge V2 → V1
- Do not treat “deploy” alone as Version 1 or Version 2 — require the explicit phrase
- Keep versions completely separate until approved release

## Objective

- Version 1 = stable production (`main`)
- Version 2 = active development (`website-v2`)
- Do not mix them
